WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.470
Meet Tansy.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.390
Tansy hands out the keys to your team’s code.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:11.330
Whoever knocks gets one: a contractor, a new hire, a reviewer who only reads.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:16.290
Months later, nobody knows who still holds a key.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:26.170
Team Access keeps one roster: a short file of who gets in, and how far.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:31.430
An audit compares the roster with real access, and changes nothing.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.310
A dry run lists every change first.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.540
Removals wait for sync mode, which asks.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.850
A typo gets a warning, and sync won’t remove half the team at once.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.410
Its tests used stand-ins.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.430
No real invites went out.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:55.330
Applying is your call.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:05.600
Team Access.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.360
See who has access.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.490
Apply the roster you intended.
